{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ গণিত (৫৫১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) If the sum of first n terms of a G.P. is S<sub>n</sub> = 7(2<sup>n</sup> - 1), then the common ratio is:", "option1": "1", "option2": "2", "option3": "3", "option4": "4", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div>\r\n<div>This matches the form:</div>\r\n<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_194247.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"358\" height=\"57\"></div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Evaluate: <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195245.png\" width=\"276\" height=\"98\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195449.png\" width=\"119\" height=\"93\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195534.png\" width=\"106\" height=\"104\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195545.png\" width=\"117\" height=\"115\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195554.png\" width=\"84\" height=\"118\" alt=\"\">", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_195958.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"388\" height=\"56\"><br>​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_200011.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"497\" height=\"148\"></div>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) A series where each term cancels with a part of the next term is called:", "option1": "Arithmetic Series", "option2": "Geometric Series", "option3": "Telescoping Series", "option4": "Harmonic Series", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>A series where each term cancels with a part of the next term is called telescoping series.</div>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) The sum of the series 5 + 8 + 11 +.........+ 50 is-", "option1": "510", "option2": "550", "option3": "440", "option4": "660", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>here   a=5, d=3, l=50<br>​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_gt6mtyV.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"364\" height=\"130\"></div>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) For geometric progression <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_200355.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"288\" height=\"133\"> is true when", "option1": "r &lt; 1", "option2": "r &gt; 1", "option3": "r &gt; 0", "option4": "none", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_200448.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"618\" height=\"169\"></div>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) The sum 2 + 4 + 6 +.................+ 2n equals:", "option1": "n(n + 1)", "option2": "2n(n + 1)", "option3": "n<sup>2</sup>", "option4": "n<sup>2</sup>+ 1", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>S<sub>n</sub>= (n/2) [2a + (n - 1)d] = n(n + 1)</div>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) sin10°+ sin20°+.............+ sin100° equals:", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_201026.png\" width=\"167\" height=\"61\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_201039.png\" width=\"151\" height=\"56\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "None", "option4": "0", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>​​​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_at_Aug_16_11-52-39.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"578\" height=\"269\"></div>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) the nth term of tan<sup>- 1</sup> (1/3) + tan<sup>- 1</sup> (2/9) + ....", "option1": "tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n</sup> - tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n -1</sup>", "option2": "tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n-1</sup> - tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n</sup>", "option3": "tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n</sup> + tan<sup>-1</sup> 2<sup>n -1</sup>", "option4": "none", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_201718.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"685\" height=\"55\"></div>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) A polynomial has 4 sign changes in P(x). The number of positive real roots can be:", "option1": "4, 2, or 0", "option2": "3", "option3": "1 only", "option4": "None", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>\r\n<div>For positive real roots:<br>From Descarte’s rule of sign change </div>\r\n<div>Count the number of sign changes in  which is 4</div>\r\n<div>Each sign change corresponds to:</div>\r\n<div>• a possible real root, or<br>• Fewer roots than the count by a multiple of 2.</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) For P(x) = x<sup>3</sup>- 6x<sup>2</sup>+ 11x - 6, number of sign changes:", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "2", "option4": "3", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div>Here number of sign change is = 3<br>​+x<sup>3</sup> to - 6x<sup>2</sup>, then - 6x<sup>2</sup> to + 11x, then  +11x  to - 6</div>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) After synthetic division of x<sup>3</sup>- 3x<sup>2</sup>+ 3x - 1 by x - 1, the quotient is:", "option1": "x<sup>2</sup>- 2x + 1", "option2": "x<sup>2</sup>+ 2x + 1", "option3": "x<sup>2 </sup>- 3x + 1", "option4": "x<sup>2</sup>- x + 2", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>x<sup>3</sup>- 3x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3x - 1<br>​= x<sup>2</sup>(x - 1) - 2x(x-1) + 1(x - 1)<br>​= (x - 1)(x<sup>2</sup>- 2x + 1)<br>​So (x<sup>2 </sup>- 2x + 1) is the quotient</div>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Synthetic division is most efficient when divisor is:", "option1": "Quadratic", "option2": "x + a", "option3": "x<sup>2</sup>+ ax + b", "option4": "Cubic", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div>Synthetic division is most efficient when divisor is linear </div>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) In synthetic division, if the remainder is 0, then:", "option1": "The value is not a root", "option2": "The divisor is a factor", "option3": "The polynomial is even", "option4": "The polynomial is odd", "answer": "2", "exp": "<div>In synthetic division, if the remainder is 0, then the divisor is a factor</div>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) A polynomial equation of degree 5 can have how many complex roots at most?", "option1": "3", "option2": "4", "option3": "5", "option4": "6", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>A polynomial equation of degree n can have how many complex roots at most n.</div>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) The polynomial P(x) = x<sup>2</sup>+ 4x + 4 has:", "option1": "Two distinct real roots", "option2": "Two complex roots", "option3": "One real repeated root", "option4": "No roots", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>\r\n<div>Discriminant, D = 4<sup>2 </sup>- 4.1.4 = 0  </div>\r\n<div>One real repeated root</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) The remainder when P(x) = x<sup>3</sup>+ 2x<sup>2</sup>- x + 5 is divided by x - 1 is:", "option1": "7", "option2": "- 7", "option3": "5", "option4": "0", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>Remainder  = P(1) = 1<sup>3 </sup>+ 2.1<sup>2 </sup>- 1 + 5 = 7</div>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) The degree of (x<sup>2</sup>+ 1)(x - 2 + x<sup>3</sup>) is:", "option1": "2", "option2": "3", "option3": "5", "option4": "6", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>Degree is sum of highest degrees: 2 + 3 = 5</div>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) If α, β are roots of 3x<sup>2</sup> - 2x + 1 = 0, the equation whose roots are α<sup>2</sup>, β<sup>2</sup> is:", "option1": "3x<sup>2</sup>+ 2x - 1=0", "option2": "9x<sup>2</sup>+ 4x + 1=0", "option3": "3x<sup>2</sup>- 4x + 1=0", "option4": "9x<sup>2</sup>+ 2x + 1=0", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div><br>​<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_203452.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"488\" height=\"175\"></div>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) If 2x<sup>2</sup>+ 2x - k is a full square, then what is the value of k?", "option1": "3/2", "option2": "- (3/2)", "option3": "1/2", "option4": "- (1/2)", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div>\r\n<div>Since 2x<sup>2 </sup>+ 2x - k is a square then discriminant of 2x<sup>2 </sup>+ 2x - k = 0 is = 0</div>\r\n<div>So, 2<sup>2</sup>- 4.2.(- k) = 0 or, k = - (1/2)</div>\r\n</div>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) What is the maximum value of 5 + 3x - x<sup>2</sup>?&nbsp;", "option1": "3", "option2": "11/4", "option3": "29/4", "option4": "27/4", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_203937.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"262\" height=\"250\"></div>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) For what value of p, x<sup>2</sup>+ px + 1 = 0 has complex roots?", "option1": "- 2 ≤ p ≤2", "option2": "- 4 ≤ p ≤ 4", "option3": "- 2 &lt; p &lt; 2", "option4": "- 4 &lt; p &lt; 4", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div>Here x<sup>2 </sup>+ px + 1=0</div>\r\n<div>Now for complex roots,</div>\r\n<div>D = 0</div>\r\n<div>Or, P<sup>2</sup>- 4.1.1&lt;0</div>\r\n<div>Or, p<sup>2 </sup>&lt; 4</div>\r\n<div>Or, -  2</div>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) 5x<sup>2</sup>- kx + 9 = 0 has one root which is equal to 5 times of second root, what is the value of k?", "option1": "12", "option2": "16", "option3": "18", "option4": "9", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_204821.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"580\" height=\"300\"></div>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) If the roots 3x<sup>2</sup>- 10x + k = 0 has roots a and 1/a , what is the value of k?", "option1": "3", "option2": "1", "option3": "0", "option4": "- 3", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_205129.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"450\" height=\"108\"></div>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/1_901cvY4.png\" width=\"712\" height=\"63\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "0.5", "option2": "0", "option3": "1", "option4": "none", "answer": "3", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/qwe.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"808\" height=\"508\"></div>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Which one of the following is the quadratic equation having root 5 + 3i?", "option1": "x<sup>2</sup>- 10x + 34 = 0", "option2": "x<sup>2</sup>- 10x - 34 = 0", "option3": "x<sup>2</sup>+ 10x - 34 = 0", "option4": "x - 5 = 3i", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>If one root is, a = 5 + 3i, other root is b=5 - 3i<br>​So the equation is, x<sup>2</sup>-(a + b)x + ab=0<br>​Or, x<sup>2</sup>- (5 + 3i + 5 - 3i)x + (5 + 3i)(5 - 3i) = 0<br>​Or, x<sup>2</sup>- 10x + 34 = 0</div>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) If one root of a quadratic equation is, 1/(2 - √5) find the other one-", "option1": "- 2 - √5", "option2": "2 + √5", "option3": "2 - √5", "option4": "- 2 + √5", "answer": "4", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_210903.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"516\" height=\"113\"></div>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Evaluate: <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_210937.png\" width=\"250\" height=\"87\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "0", "option2": "1", "option3": "- 2", "option4": "2", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211144.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"696\" height=\"156\"></div>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) In a telescoping series, which terms usually remain?", "option1": "First and last", "option2": "All terms", "option3": "Middle terms", "option4": "Only one term", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>By the definition, a telescoping series is one where consecutive terms cancel out, leaving only a few terms at the beginning and end.</div>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) What is the nth term of the series <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211556.png\" width=\"523\" height=\"53\" alt=\"\">", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211617.png\" width=\"264\" height=\"76\" alt=\"\">", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211627.png\" width=\"245\" height=\"74\" alt=\"\">", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211634.png\" width=\"232\" height=\"68\" alt=\"\">", "option4": "None", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211726.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"588\" height=\"122\"></div>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Result of dividing x<sup>2</sup> - 3x + 2 by x - 1:", "option1": "Quotient: x - 2, Remainder: 0", "option2": "Quotient: x + 2, R: 1", "option3": "Quotient: x - 1, R: 2", "option4": "None", "answer": "1", "exp": "<div>Now, <img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Screenshot_2025-08-14_211920.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"222\" height=\"49\">no, remainder left.\r\n<div>Else we can use synthetic division method. </div>\r\n</div>"}]}, "_source": "archive-question-subject", "_exam_id": 12291, "custom_field": "প্রতি প্রশ্নের মান ১ ও ভুল উত্তরের জন্য ০.৫০ কাটা যাবে।", "exam_time": "1800000", "is_omr": true, "omr_time": "2100000", "examname": "Aug 15, 2025", "type": "Math-Sub-551", "payment": "BALANCE_NOT"}